# Assist / Voice Pipeline Dialog

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

The Assist dialog lets people give Home Assistant a request by typing or speaking, and shows the conversation. A pipeline is the set of speech and conversation services Assist uses. Civica does not change how Assist listens or acts. It changes the colours and shapes of the dialog surface that the Civica theme reaches.

This page owns the dialog and the chat as components. For what to show while Assist listens, works and answers, see [Assist and voice](../home-assistant/assist-and-voice.html). For dialog focus, closing and returning focus, see [Dialogs](dialogs.html).

This page covers:

- Assist / Voice Pipeline Dialog
  - `ha-voice-command-dialog`
  - `ha-assist-chat`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

- A header with a close button, the title, a pipeline menu, a link to Assist settings for administrators and a help button.
- The chat: messages from the person on one side and from Home Assistant on the other, a text field for typing, and a send or microphone button.
- A spinner while the dialog loads, and an error alert if it cannot.

